@startuml reconcile
title Companion to M-DP1 / M-DP2: v0 / v1 reconciliation (draft)
participant "Dispatcher core\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher" as D
database "Dispatcher-owned journal, effects,\ninput/agent/run records and claims" as J
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; account ledger / stop evidence" as H
participant "Credential broker\nunprivileged; binding / grant / lease owner" as B
participant "Process evidence\nsupervisor service UID / executor agent UID" as P
D -> J : lock; replay journal; list non-terminal records
loop each allocation / execution, state by state (§7.1)
  D -> H : observe generation, create effect, start/termination receipts
  D -> B : observe binding by effect ID
  D -> P : observe supervisor registration / execution identity
  alt any observation unknown or contradictory
    D -> J : retain state and capacity; retry observation later\nnever relaunch or declare cleanup successful
  else provisioning; create effect unknown before query
    D -> J : use known ledger answer; never create again until known
  else provisioning; account present; bind known absent after query
    alt request still valid
      D -> B : bind with journaled effect ID
    else invalid authority/window
      alt ordinary allocation
        D -> J : retire; applicable cleanup must be confirmed
      else standing allocation
        D -> J : retain pending; await operator-signed decision; no re-creation
      end
    end
  else idle; binding known absent; ordinary not expired or standing
    D -> D : fresh authority checks
    alt authority valid
      D -> B : rebind
    else authority gone
      alt ordinary allocation
        D -> J : retire
      else standing allocation
        D -> J : no forward execution; await operator-signed decision; no retirement
      end
    end
  else claimed; no supervisor registration
    D -> J : mark execution claim absent; no later launch
  else launching; receipt unknown
    D -> J : wait for receipt/launcher answer; cancel also waits; never relaunch
  else started; supervisor known absent
    D -> H : exec.stop {same E-stop, generation, execution_id}
    H --> D : termination receipt only after no process remains
    D -> J : record lost after confirmation
  else stopping; termination receipt missing
    D -> H : repeat exec.stop with same effect ID
  else retiring / cleaning; pending authorised effects
    D -> B : repeat applicable unbind with same effect ID
    D -> H : retire only after unbind confirmed; same retire effect ID
    D -> J : applicable one-shot identity cleanup after retirement (§14)\nterminal only after all required confirmations
  end
end
note over D,J
  v0 invocation, v1 startup/periodic, explicit reconcile (§7.1).
  v0 internal service-only sweep every minute; v1 daemon internal (§7.2).
  Standing: no expires_at or lifetime quota; sweep never expires it.
  Standing executions: no max_runtime quota or deadline, including after recovery.
  Sweep never stops them for runtime; ordinary executions keep 4 h / 12 h,
  and sweep stops them through exec.stop when their runtime deadline elapses (§7.2).
  Standing retirement/re-creation requires operator-signed record (§5.4).
  An absent account never authorises automatic standing re-creation.
  Intent is journaled before every external effect (§4.1).
  Refused cleanup stays pending; unknown is never known absent (§4.6).
  Keeper API and broker service UID spelling are unspecified in spec §§14, 3.1.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#71-reconciliation §7.1 reconciliation]]
  [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#46-observations §4.6 observations]] / §§5.4, 9, 14
endlegend
@enduml
